  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Established in 2015, Siasa Place is a youth-led and youth-focused civic-tech organization that is building confidence, skills, competencies, and institutional structures necessary for meaningful and dignified participation of young people in politics, governance, and the civic life in Kenya. Inspired by the constitutional promise of the right to public participation and convinced of young people&#x2019;s interest, potential, and capacity to influence decisions that affect them, Siasa Place is leveraging the technology to expand the reach and quality of young peoples&#x2019; engagement in the social, economic, civic, and political life of their communities. Siasa Place aims to advance its strategic vision and strengthen its institutional resilience and capacity to quickly respond to emerging needs and emergencies as well as extend its actions and contextual response. (Strategy: Inclusive Governance)</narrative>
  </description>
